I need to fix the issue in `stats.py` where the `mean()` function uses integer division (`//`) which truncates decimal values. This causes the summary to show truncated values instead of proper decimal averages.

The fix is to change the division operator from `//` to `/` to perform floating-point division.

stats.py
```
def mean(xs):
    return sum(xs) / len(xs)
```

This change will ensure that the mean calculation returns a floating-point value instead of an integer, which will correctly produce decimal results in the summary output. When combined with the existing `summary()` function in `report.py`, this will fix the test to pass.
